---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionRule from '../components/SectionRule.astro';
import PhotoGrid from '../components/PhotoGrid.astro';
import { site, principles, education, awayGallery } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={site.intro}
>
  <section class="page-head grid-backdrop">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label label--accent">About</p>
      <h1 class="page-head__title">{site.name}</h1>
      <p class="page-head__sub measure-wide">{site.role}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div
      class:list={[
        'container',
        'about__layout',
        { 'about__layout--solo': !site.portrait },
      ]}
    >
      {
        site.portrait && (
          <div class="about__portrait">
            <img
              src={site.portrait}
              alt={`${site.name}, portrait`}
              width="800"
              height="1000"
              loading="eager"
            />
          </div>
        )
      }

      <div class="about__bio prose measure">
        <p>
          I am a backend architect and engineering leader with fifteen years
          building software — most of it in the .NET ecosystem, and the last
          eight scaling high-stakes fintech infrastructure.
        </p>
        <p>
          I was hired at Bitcoin IRA as its first C# engineer, joining behind
          the solutions architect and spending four years building the digital
          asset trading platform — learning the iDesign approach by practising
          it rather than reading about it. Over the following four years I moved
          from technical lead to engineering manager and backend architecture
          lead, ending up as one of four architects and technical leads on the
          architecture review board, owning backend architecture for my team of
          six engineers: guiding them through their service contracts, refining
          them, and presenting them for final review.
        </p>
        <p>
          The work I am proudest of from that period is Instant Settlement —
          an in-house double-entry accounting ledger that became the platform's
          source of truth for balances, demoting the external ledger to an
          isolated downstream backup and pulling the surrounding systems and
          operational workflows onto it. Alongside it: limit order trading, a
          real-time compliance platform, and three acquisitions consolidating
          into one platform.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since March 2026 I have been working independently. It started as a
          deliberate sabbatical, the first three months of it in Brazil, and has
          become a heavy competition flying season alongside building a new
          application end to end with agents doing the writing and the
          reviewing. The stretch AI-first never reached at Retired.com was the
          human one — writing contracts, reviewing them, reviewing pull
          requests — and much of that was landing on me, which is why it is the
          part I am working on now: whether autonomous agents can
          hold precision, decoupling, and long-term quality there under real
          velocity, rather than quietly trading them away for speed.
        </p>
        <p>
          I hold a bachelor's degree in computer science from {education.school}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionRule index="01" label="What I believe" />
      <ul class="principles">
        {
          principles.map((principle, i) => (
            <li class="principle" data-reveal data-reveal-delay={i * 70}>
              <h3 class="principle__title">{principle.title}</h3>
              <p class="principle__body">{principle.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionRule index="02" label="Away from the keyboard" />
      <div class="prose measure">
        <p>
          I fly cross-country and competition paragliding — enough of it that it
          has <a href="/flying/">its own section</a>. It turns out to be the
          same discipline as engineering wearing different clothes: you plan
          carefully, you commit, and then you are honest with yourself
          afterwards about what actually happened.
        </p>
        <p>
          Right now that means a season that has run more or less continuously
          since March — Brazil, then California, Oregon, Washington and British
          Columbia, and Mexico still to come — with the weeks in between spent
          in Nevada, outside or in the terminal.
        </p>
        <p>
          Below is roughly the last couple of years of the away-from-the-desk
          half — mostly mountains and coastline, plus one cat who has been up
          more of them than most cats.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="away__photos">
        <PhotoGrid photos={awayGallery} columns={4} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionRule index="03" label="Elsewhere" />
      <ul class="elsewhere">
        {
          site.links.map((link) => (
            <li>
              <a href={link.href} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">
                {link.label} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-12);
  }

  .page-head__title {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-4);
  }

  .page-head__sub {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .about__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(14rem, 20rem) 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* Collapses to one column until a portrait is set in site.ts, so the live
     site never shows an empty placeholder. */
  .about__layout--solo {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .about__portrait {
    position: sticky;
    top: 6rem;
  }

  .about__portrait img {
    inline-size: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .away__photos {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-12);
  }

  .principles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(15rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8) var(--space-6);
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .principle {
    padding-block-start: var(--space-4);
    border-block-start: var(--hairline) solid var(--rule);
  }

  .principle__title {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
  }

  .principle__body {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .elsewhere {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .elsewhere a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-block-end: var(--hairline) solid var(--rule-strong);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-1);
  }

  .elsewhere a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .about__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-12);
    }

    .about__portrait {
      position: static;
      max-inline-size: 18rem;
    }
  }
</style>
